00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:31.450
Simple, right?

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.200
Koi...

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.700
Were you that hungry?

00:07:34.700 --> 00:07:35.580
What?

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:37.950
Well, you just nommed
at the line out of nowhere!

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:42.370
No, I just made them wet to
avoid any heat from the friction.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:45.380
Lines get weaker with heat, so...

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:46.710
Oho.

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:48.920
You can use the river water
to make them wet, too.

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:52.550
Is it better to make them wet
when you attach the fly, too?

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:53.430
Yeah.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:55.100
Got it!

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:01.640
I suddenly remembered
Hiyori impersonating a fishy.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:02.690
Wait, what?

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:04.600
When we went fishing
at the mountain stream,

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:08.730
every time I would cast my line, she would
impersonate a fish and go, "Chomp!"

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:10.400
It look liked Hiyori was having

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.280
way more fun watching than me,
who was actually fishing.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:15.160
I see.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:18.080
Okay, I'm off. Thanks a bunch, Koi!

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:19.950
Good luck out there.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:28.670
It looks like they're having
a hard time catching one.

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:32.300
Well... The wind's not blowing
right now, so it might be difficult.

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:34.050
Really?

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:37.350
It's easier to trick the fish
when you have a slight breeze

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:41.390
and ripples going on in the water
because they can't see the line very well.

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:43.230
I see...

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:47.770
Um...

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:50.280
You three seem to get along really well.

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:53.030
Hm? Yeah, I guess so.

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:55.860
You've seen how Koharu is and Ya--

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:58.490
Hiyori and I have been
friends since we were little.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:00.120
Since you were little?

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:05.830
Yup. Our moms were friends
before we were even born.

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:10.420
So our oldest memories together were
basically us together at nursery school.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:11.460
Want some?

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:13.920
Th-Then...

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:19.050
Doesn't it make you feel uneasy seeing
Hiyori and Koharu getting along so well?

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:20.260
Huh?

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:25.230
I've been feeling so uneasy lately.

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:28.150
Whenever I see Futaba getting
along with someone else, I can't help

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:31.270
but wonder if she's having more fun
with them than she does with me.

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:35.650
But I want to stay
as Futaba's best friend...

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:42.330
I wonder if Futaba will hate me
if she finds out I'm thinking this.

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:45.120
Well, aren't you absolutely adorable...?

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:45.830
"Pockitto
Strawberry Flavor"

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:47.540
"Pockitto
Strawberry Flavor"
Here you go.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:49.710
"Pockitto
Strawberry Flavor"
Thank you...

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:50.040
"Pockitto
Strawberry Flavor"

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:54.010
Her best friend, huh...

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:56.380
But...

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.890
Being her best friend
can get heavy sometimes.

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:00.220
Huh?

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:05.730
Don't worry. She seems to be having
the most fun when she's with you, Aiko.

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:06.560
Huh?

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:09.770
I think for Futaba,
you're a friend she can have fun with,

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:12.570
but also one who she
can feel at ease around.

00:10:12.570 --> 00:10:15.820
I-I hope that's the case...

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:26.540
Stare...

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:29.960
Burst mode...

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:34.090
Don't let your line get too loose!

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:35.460
Okay!

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:45.680
I've never seen a rainbow
trout jump around so much!

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:48.560
Great job catching it
without letting it go.

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:54.020
Aiko! I caught one!

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:55.730
Great job, Futaba!

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:57.940
I'll be right over!

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:00.740
That's amazing!

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:03.030
Thanks, Aiko.

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:08.200
It can get pretty rough pretending
that you know everything.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:10.120
Koi...

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:13.340
Is there a name for the phenomenon
where you only get a bite

00:11:13.340 --> 00:11:16.340
every single time you look away?

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:18.630
Don't give up, Fly-Fishing Woman.

00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:26.680
Futaba, Aiko! I'm going to put
you two in charge of dinner prep!

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:28.430
Have you two ever cooked before?

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:31.020
I help out my mom all the time.

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:34.310
I've only made miso soup
in a cooking class...

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:37.480
Well, if you've made miso soup before,
you'll totally be fine.

00:11:37.480 --> 00:11:39.570
Today, we're going to
use the rainbow trout

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:42.410
we caught and make the Russian dish, ukha.

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:43.910
Ukha?

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:46.870
I knew we were going to the mountains,
so I searched the internet

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:51.160
for a dish that'd help
keep us warm. It's a fish soup.

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:52.960
Okay, let's get started.

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:54.830
Okay!

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:56.800
Once you put the veggies into the pot,

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:59.590
put the big chunks of
rainbow trout in there, too.

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:03.090
Then we'll add bay leaves
and some chopped dill stalks.

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:04.050
Dill?

00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:08.600
It's a herb. Then we'll add in
some water and let it stew.

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:14.020
Koharu, do you mind if I use the
remaining rainbow trout for breakfast?

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:15.560
Sure!

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:19.650
By the way, Koharu,
did you end up catching some?

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:22.240
W-Well, I caught a few...

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:26.490
It's not as impressive as Hiyori's,
but I caught one that was this big.

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:28.120
Huh...

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:31.580
You know, in Russia,
there's a proverb that says,

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:34.670
"Keep your hands tied when
you're talking about fishing."

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:36.540
Do you know what it's trying to say?

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:39.000
Uh... Because people might start fighting?

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:43.930
Nope. Whenever fishermen talk
about the size of the fish they caught

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:47.010
the space between their hands
just keeps getting bigger.

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:50.470
You're... You're such
a meanie, you know that?!

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:52.100
Ow...

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:56.900
Okay, fine. I was only able to
catch a smol baby rainbow trout.

00:12:56.900 --> 00:13:01.940
I feel so bad when I try to get
the hook out of a baby one...

00:13:01.940 --> 00:13:03.490
S-Sorry...

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:08.030
K-Koharu, the veggies have softened.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:12.160
Now, we'll had some salt
and pepper for the seasoning.

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:16.330
Once we pour the soup into bowls, we'll
float a thinly sliced lime at the top.

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:19.750
And once you sprinkle in some dill leaves
that you've ground up with your hands...

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:24.050
The ukha is complete! You can
even add some butter if you'd like.

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:26.930
Let's eat!

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:32.060
It's so good!

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:34.810
Yeah, it's great!

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:36.310
What a gentle flavor.

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:38.440
The potatoes are so hot.

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:40.150
It warms you right up.

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:42.860
Koharu, this is really good.

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:45.780
It is.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:49.200
Well, Futaba and Aiko
worked hard to make it for us.

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:54.080
I made us a dish for dinner, too.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:56.870
Roast beef?! Ooh, fancy!

00:13:56.870 --> 00:14:02.460
I also smoked some cheese, edamame,
and other things to go with our drinks.

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:07.010
I also made some hot wine,
so please, help yourselves.

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:09.760
Did I die and go to heaven?

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:13.310
Sis, make sure you don't drink too much...

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:17.190
I was hoping I could feed you
guys some freshly-caught duck,

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:20.310
but I won't be able
to hunt until next month.

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:22.610
I'd love to see you catch one!

00:14:22.610 --> 00:14:24.440
I'd also like to join in.

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:26.570
M-Me, too...

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:31.660
Sure. But my car is tiny,
so I'll only be able to take one of you.

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:35.330
She's going to be
selling feathers at my shop,

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:38.460
so I should get priority to go.

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:43.170
That has nothing to do
with this! I asked first!

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:46.130
--Um... I'll be going more than once,
so I can just take you all eventually...

00:14:46.130 --> 00:14:47.260
--Calm down, you two.
--Um... I'll be going more than once,
so I can just take you all eventually...

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:48.470
--Calm down, you two.

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:52.350
How about the one who catches the most
fish on our next fishing trip gets to go?

00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:53.350
That'll be fair.

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:56.980
That's not fair at all! You have
the biggest advantage, Hiyori!

00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:59.060
Th-That's not true...

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:01.060
She's trying to get a lead on us!

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:03.480
I am not.

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:09.280
Oh, come on, you three.
Don't trouble Ms. Miyano like this.

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:30.680
Good morning...

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:31.840
Morning.

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:35.470
Were the fish on the tarp dried overnight?

00:15:35.470 --> 00:15:37.520
Nah, I just put them out.

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:42.190
I let them soak in some brine overnight.

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:45.110
Once they dry, I'll be smoking them,
so look forward to it.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:46.360
Sure.

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:49.190
Hiyori came by a moment ago
and went fishing.

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:51.450
I see...

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:56.410
May I have some of that hot water?
I wanted to make some coffee.

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:57.740
Sure.

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:03.830
That's a lot of sugar.

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:07.130
Hiyori can't drink coffee
unless it's sweetened.

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:09.920
It'd be even better if we had any milk.

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:12.880
Oh, I brought some. Want me to warm it up?

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:14.640
Thank you very much.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:17.430
You're like an older sister, Koi.

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:21.430
You're far more responsible
than the other two your age.

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:25.360
I wouldn't say that...

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:36.700
And then, and then...

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:41.790
Ryo was crying, but I didn't cry at all!

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:44.170
I see. Well, aren't you a good boy?

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:47.750
Ah! It's Yamahi!

00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:49.800
Taking them home from nursery school?

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:51.970
Yup. What about you?

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:56.390
Well... I thought I'd look out
at the sea as I headed home.

00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:02.930
Oh, yeah. I overheard our moms talking,

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:06.100
but I guess she's getting
married again. Congratulations.

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:08.230
Huh? Getting married again?

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:11.400
Um... Your mom...

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:13.990
O-Oh, really?

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:20.990
Sissy, I gotta go pee!

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:25.170
Wh-What?! Dang it. I asked you
if you had to go before we left!

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:26.710
Yeah!

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:30.460
Koi, why don't you take him
to the public restroom nearby?

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:33.840
I'll take Niji home for you.

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:36.890
Niji, let's go home together.

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:38.550
Sure!

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:39.800
B-But...

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:41.220
Sissy...

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:44.560
Okay. Thanks, Yamahi.

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:46.140
Sure.

00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:08.880
Yamahi.

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:10.380
Koi.

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:15.010
Here's your café au lait.

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:16.760
Thanks.

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:21.390
It's so sweet and yummy.

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:27.100
If our dads came here, they would've
been out fishing bright and early, too.

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:28.440
Yeah.

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:34.530
As I was casting my line, I randomly
remembered you saying congratulations

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:37.740
about my mom getting remarried.

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:40.740
I'm so sorry about that...

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:42.830
Huh? Why are you apologizing?

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:48.460
Well, I mean... I ended up telling
you something you didn't know.

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:55.710
But if you hadn't mentioned anything,
my mom wouldn't have remarried.

00:18:55.710 --> 00:18:58.840
After you mentioned that,
I asked my mom about it...

00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:01.050
And she said she'd met
someone through your mom

00:19:01.050 --> 00:19:03.560
and he had a daughter that was my age,

00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:06.850
so she was talking to him a lot.

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:13.020
I think my mom was worried about how
I'd feel and wasn't planning to remarry.

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:17.530
But my mom held back so much
and went through so much...

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:22.070
So I thought she needed someone who
she could relate to and could support her.

00:19:22.070 --> 00:19:26.830
She's always just been "Mom" to me.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:30.420
So I told her that she
should get remarried.

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:34.750
If you hadn't told me about
my mom possibly getting remarried,

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:38.300
we wouldn't have been able to go fishing
and camping with a group again like this.

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:40.470
But...

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:43.550
That's just in hindsight.

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:48.430
I try to act all mature, but deep down,
I'm still just a thoughtless child.

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:53.060
The deeper I try to go,
the more I hurt those important to me.

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:55.110
Then I'm just...

00:19:55.110 --> 00:19:57.360
That's not true!

00:19:57.360 --> 00:20:03.070
It's because you congratulated us that
I was able to take a step forward, too.

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:07.290
I was trying to avoid a lot
of things back then.

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:11.750
Like my mom or having kids
in class worry about me...

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:13.790
Or my dad...

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:14.880
But...

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:17.250
It's because you said, "Congratulations,"

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:20.590
that I thought it was
okay for me to feel this way.

00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:25.680
I felt a little lonely about
everything changing around me,

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:28.810
but you didn't change at all.

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:32.020
That made me so happy.

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:33.940
The reason I'm able to smile right now

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:36.690
is because you've been by my side.

00:20:36.690 --> 00:20:39.070
So...

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:42.150
Um... What were we talking about again?

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:45.660
Hiyori, you're starting
to turn into Koharu.

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:47.450
Huh?

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:53.290
But... I think you might've been
like that when we were little.

00:20:53.290 --> 00:20:55.830
Are you trying to say
Koharu's a little kid?

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:59.380
I'm not going to deny that.

00:20:59.380 --> 00:21:01.380
There you are!

00:21:01.380 --> 00:21:03.380
Breakfast is ready!

00:21:03.380 --> 00:21:04.840
Koharu.

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:07.600
What were you two talking
about all by yourselves?

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:14.390
It's a secret.

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:16.400
How dare you?!

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:20.900
What an insolent little brat you are!
You're not gonna get away with that!

00:21:23.990 --> 00:21:27.530
Put the smoked rainbow trout on the
baguette with whatever veggies you'd like.

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:28.830
Okay.

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:31.450
I'm going to put a lot
of tomatoes on mine!

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:35.330
I'm sure this camping trip is going
to be a memorable one for them.

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:37.540
Hopefully it's a great memory.

00:21:37.540 --> 00:21:42.050
I just want to be some tree
watching over them from afar.

00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:44.300
What the hell are you talking about?

00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:47.300
What's your oldest memory?

00:21:47.300 --> 00:21:49.180
Hm...

00:21:49.180 --> 00:21:53.810
When the goldfish I had ended up
eating their babies... I think.

00:21:53.810 --> 00:21:57.230
And you're okay with
your life starting there?

00:21:57.230 --> 00:22:00.820
I think mine is when Koi
attached a fly onto my line.

00:22:00.820 --> 00:22:04.030
Wow, really?

00:22:04.030 --> 00:22:06.240
What about you, Koi?

00:22:06.240 --> 00:22:07.740
That's a secret, too.

00:22:07.740 --> 00:22:09.910
Oh, you're such an insolent brat!

00:22:09.910 --> 00:22:11.990
Why do you keep saying that word?

00:22:11.990 --> 00:22:16.790
Koharu's been watching
a lot of old dramas lately.

00:22:16.790 --> 00:22:18.710
Absolutely unacceptable!

00:22:18.710 --> 00:22:21.500
Come on, now. You've got some
bread bits on your mouth.

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:23.170
How dare you?!

00:22:30.140 --> 00:22:32.760
<i>Even if you don't say anything</i>

00:22:32.760 --> 00:22:38.480
<i>I know how you're feeling and</i>
<i>when you're lying or telling the truth</i>

00:22:38.480 --> 00:22:41.150
<i>Even if you don't do anything</i>

00:22:41.150 --> 00:22:46.150
<i>Just being next to you</i>
<i>makes the day brighter</i>

00:22:46.150 --> 00:22:50.370
<i>The reason I've always loved the ocean</i>

00:22:50.370 --> 00:22:55.120
<i>Is because you were always by my side</i>

00:22:55.120 --> 00:22:58.330
<i>The way we laugh is becoming similar</i>

00:22:58.330 --> 00:23:03.460
<i>It's almost like we're cider</i>

00:23:03.460 --> 00:23:07.670
<i>Bubble, bubble, our laughter combines</i>

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:11.970
<i>Bubble, bubble, then floats up</i>
<i>and pops together</i>

00:23:11.970 --> 00:23:20.230
<i>We gather up the light and</i>
<i>gain even more precious things</i>

00:23:20.230 --> 00:23:24.480
<i>Bubble, bubble, our laughter combines</i>

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:28.820
<i>Bubble, bubble, then floats up</i>
<i>and pops together</i>

00:23:28.820 --> 00:23:33.780
<i>May a present where we can</i>
<i>laugh about the past and future</i>

00:23:33.780 --> 00:23:39.910
<i>Always be right here</i>

00:23:41.460 --> 00:23:46.460
<i>May a present where we can</i>
<i>laugh about the past and future</i>

00:23:46.460 --> 00:23:52.840
<i>Always be right here</i>

00:23:54.970 --> 00:23:55.720
"Next Time"

00:23:55.720 --> 00:23:58.770
"Next Time"

00:23:55.720 --> 00:23:58.770
You have all kinds of
different flies, Hiyori.

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:03.440
"Next Time"

00:23:58.770 --> 00:24:03.440
Yup. A cicada, a dragonfly, a bee,
an ant, a grasshopper, and a spider.

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:04.810
"Next Time"

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:04.810
This one's a stinkbug!

00:24:04.810 --> 00:24:07.320
"Next Time"

00:24:04.810 --> 00:24:07.320
You sure know a lot about bugs
when you hate them so much.

00:24:07.320 --> 00:24:09.900
"Next Time"

00:24:07.320 --> 00:24:09.900
W-Well, these aren't real!
